  "label": "Woman as the 'appliance' that needs to be 'hit' to fix problems",
  "description": "The text 'everyone knows hitting appliances that stop working, sometimes fixes the problem' is mapped onto the visual of the woman with blood on her lip. The analogy suggests that the woman is being treated as an appliance — something that must be physically 'hit' or subjected to violence to 'fix' problems, implying she is expected to be the solution through harm. The visual of her injury (blood on lip) literalizes the violent 'fixing' implied by the text, reinforcing the misogynistic trope that women are expected to endure or cause harm to resolve issues.",
